# Implementation Plan — FlowGuard Incident Dashboard Analytics Enhancements

Branch: `incident-tracking-latest`. All paths below are absolute to `C:\Fullstack Assignment (FlowGuard)\FlowGuard`. This plan reflects direct inspection of the current code (not just the background brief) — several corrections/decisions below were found during that inspection and are called out in Section 6.

---

## 1. Backend changes

### 1.1 Model — `server/models/IncidentLog.js`
Add one nullable field after `resolutionStatus` (line 33, before `notes`):
```js
resolvedAt: {
    type: DataTypes.DATE,
    allowNull: true,
    defaultValue: null
},
```
Sequelize maps this camelCase attribute straight to a quoted `"resolvedAt"` column (no `underscored` option set on this model), matching the existing `"tokenVersion"`-style precedent in `20260729_sync_missing_columns.sql`.

### 1.2 Migration — new file `server/migrations/20260803_add_incident_resolved_at.sql`
Follow the exact header/BEGIN/COMMIT style of the two existing files:
```sql
-- 20260803_add_incident_resolved_at.sql
--
-- Purpose
--   Adds incident_logs."resolvedAt" (TIMESTAMPTZ, nullable) backing the new
--   Mean-Time-To-Resolve analytics on the Incident Dashboard's Deep Analytics
--   subpage. Stamped by PATCH /api/incident/:id when resolutionStatus
--   transitions into a terminal state (Cleared / False Positive) — see
--   server/routes/incident.js.
--
-- Safety
--   * Idempotent: ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS.
--   * Non-destructive, no backfill: existing already-Cleared incidents get
--     resolvedAt = NULL and are simply excluded from MTTR until a new
--     terminal transition happens post-deploy. (updatedAt is NOT used as a
--     backfill proxy — it is touched by unrelated edits like notes changes
--     after resolution, so it would misreport resolution time.)
--   * Does NOT depend on DB_SYNC_ALTER=true.

BEGIN;

ALTER TABLE incident_logs
    ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS "resolvedAt" TIMESTAMPTZ;

COMMIT;
```
Also add a row to `server/migrations/README.md`'s table.

### 1.3 Route — `server/routes/incident.js`

**a) `ALLOWED_STATUSES` (line 14):** add `'False Positive'`:
```js
const ALLOWED_STATUSES = ['Active', 'Investigating', 'Escalated to Security', 'Cleared', 'False Positive'];
```
`RESOLUTION_TO_ALERT_STATUS` (lines 19-24) is deliberately **left unchanged** — there is no equivalent `DetectionAlert.status` value (`VALID_STATUSES` in `detectionAlerts.js` line 22 has no "false positive" analog), so `alertUpdates.status` simply won't be set when `resolutionStatus === 'False Positive'`, which is already the route's existing safe no-op path (proven by the "notes-only update does not touch the linked alert" test). Note this explicitly as intentional, not an oversight.

**b) PATCH `/:id` (lines 210-250):** add resolvedAt stamping logic. Define once near the top:
```js
const TERMINAL_STATUSES = ['Cleared', 'False Positive'];
```
Inside the handler, after validating `resolutionStatus`, before the transaction:
```js
let resolvedAtUpdate; // undefined = don't touch; null = clear; Date = stamp
if (resolutionStatus !== undefined) {
    const enteringTerminal = TERMINAL_STATUSES.includes(resolutionStatus);
    if (enteringTerminal && !log.resolvedAt) {
        resolvedAtUpdate = new Date();
    } else if (!enteringTerminal && log.resolvedAt) {
        // Reopened from a terminal state back to Active/Investigating/Escalated —
        // clear the stamp so a future re-resolution is timed correctly.
        resolvedAtUpdate = null;
    }
}
```
Then include it in `log.update({...})`:
```js
...(resolvedAtUpdate !== undefined && { resolvedAt: resolvedAtUpdate })
```
This "clear on reopen" behavior is a genuine gap in the original spec (which only described the forward stamp) — flagged in Section 6, and implemented here for correctness.

**c) No new analytics endpoint.** See Section 1.4 for the explicit design decision.

### 1.4 Design decision: no new backend aggregation route/service (explicit choice)

`GET /api/incident` (unchanged) already returns every field needed — `source`, `confidence_score`, `resolutionStatus`, `createdAt`, and (after 1.1/1.2) `resolvedAt` — for every incident, with no attribute restriction. **Recommendation: compute all four analytics items client-side** from this existing list, in a new pure-function utils module (Section 3.4), rather than adding `server/services/incidentAnalytics.js` + a route.

Rationale/trade-off (explicitly noting both sides per the requirement):
- **Client-side (recommended for this v1):** zero backend surface added beyond the resolvedAt stamp; matches how `stats`/`sourceCounts` are already computed client-side on this exact page; trivially testable as pure functions; no risk of the new subpage's numbers disagreeing with the main dashboard's numbers (same source list).
- **Server-side (future path, not built now):** would mirror `dashboardAnalytics.js`'s `buildAlertAnalytics` pattern — worth doing if the incident list grows large enough that shipping the full row set becomes wasteful, or if `GET /` ever gains pagination (which would silently break client-side aggregation across the whole dataset). Flag this as the trigger condition for revisiting.

No change to `server/routes/dashboard.js` or `server/services/dashboardAnalytics.js` is needed.

---

## 2. Main dashboard split-bar (replaces `.inc-source-counter`)

File: `client/src/pages/IncidentDashboard.jsx`

### 2.1 Data — replace `sourceCounts` memo (lines 261-264)
```js
const sourceCounts = useMemo(() => {
  const manual = incidents.filter(i => i.source === 'Manual').length;
  const fr     = incidents.filter(i => i.source === 'Facial Recognition').length;
  // Object Detection bucket = everything that is neither Manual nor Facial
  // Recognition — mirrors sourceClass()'s existing default-else branch (line
  // 33-39) exactly, so this bar's 3 segments always sum to incidents.length
  // and always agree with the table's OD badge count. See Section 6 — real
  // `source` values in this DB include "Browser Webcam", "Uploaded Video",
  // and "SecurePi Edge Node" in addition to the 3 literal values, and a naive
  // `=== 'Object Detection'` check would under-count and desync the bar.
  const od = incidents.length - manual - fr;
  return { manual, fr, od };
}, [incidents]);
```

### 2.2 JSX — replace the source-counter block (lines 422-427)
```jsx
{/* ---- Source Split Bar ---- */}
<div
  className="inc-source-splitbar-wrap"
  role="img"
  aria-label={`Incident source breakdown: ${sourceCounts.manual} manual, ${sourceCounts.fr} facial recognition, ${sourceCounts.od} object detection.`}
>
  <div className="inc-source-splitbar">
    {sourceCounts.manual > 0 && (
      <div
        className="inc-source-segment inc-source-seg-manual"
        style={{ width: `${(sourceCounts.manual / total) * 100}%` }}
        tabIndex={0}
        title={`Manual: ${sourceCounts.manual}`}
      />
    )}
    {sourceCounts.fr > 0 && (
      <div className="inc-source-segment inc-source-seg-fr" style={{ width: `${(sourceCounts.fr / total) * 100}%` }} tabIndex={0} title={`Facial Recognition: ${sourceCounts.fr}`} />
    )}
    {sourceCounts.od > 0 && (
      <div className="inc-source-segment inc-source-seg-od" style={{ width: `${(sourceCounts.od / total) * 100}%` }} tabIndex={0} title={`Object Detection: ${sourceCounts.od}`} />
    )}
  </div>
  <div className="inc-source-legend">
    <span className="inc-source-legend-item"><span className="inc-source-legend-dot inc-source-legend-dot-manual" /> Manual ({sourceCounts.manual})</span>
    <span className="inc-source-legend-item"><span className="inc-source-legend-dot inc-source-legend-dot-fr" /> Facial Recognition ({sourceCounts.fr})</span>
    <span className="inc-source-legend-item"><span className="inc-source-legend-dot inc-source-legend-dot-od" /> Object Detection ({sourceCounts.od})</span>
  </div>
  <table className="sr-only">
    <caption>Incident source breakdown</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Count</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Manual</th><td>{sourceCounts.manual}</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Facial Recognition</th><td>{sourceCounts.fr}</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Object Detection</th><td>{sourceCounts.od}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
```
Note: `total` here must be `incidents.length` (whole dataset — the source bar is not filter-scoped in the current spec, matching that `sourceCounts` today is computed off `incidents`, not `filtered`); guard divide-by-zero when `incidents.length === 0` (render an empty/neutral state, e.g. a full-width `#2d364f` track with no segments and legend counts all 0 — don't divide by zero).

Hover/focus per segment shows `title` (mark spec: every value also reachable without hovering, via the always-visible legend counts — satisfied since counts are inline in the legend text, not hidden behind hover).

### 2.3 CSS — `client/src/css/IncidentDashboard.css`
Remove or leave-but-stop-using the old `.inc-source-counter`/`.inc-source-chip*` rules (leave them in place, unreferenced, OR delete — recommend deleting the now-dead `.inc-source-counter`, `.inc-source-chip`, `.inc-source-chip-ai`, `.inc-source-chip-manual`, `.inc-source-chip-divider` rules at lines 72-108 since nothing will reference them once the JSX is replaced). Add:
```css
.inc-source-splitbar-wrap { margin-bottom: 16px; }

.inc-source-splitbar {
  display: flex;
  height: 12px;               /* compact, within the ≤24px mark-spec cap */
  border-radius: 4px;         /* rounded only at the two outer ends */
  overflow: hidden;
  background: #2d364f;        /* empty-state track color */
}

.inc-source-segment {
  height: 100%;
  transition: filter 0.15s;
}
/* 2px surface-color gap between segments — NOT a border */
.inc-source-segment + .inc-source-segment { margin-left: 2px; }
.inc-source-segment:hover, .inc-source-segment:focus-visible {
  filter: brightness(1.15);
  outline: none;
}

.inc-source-seg-manual { background: #199e70; }
.inc-source-seg-fr     { background: #3987e5; }
.inc-source-seg-od     { background: #d95926; }

.inc-source-legend {
  display: flex;
  gap: 14px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-top: 8px;
}
.inc-source-legend-item {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 6px;
  color: #94a3b8;
  font-size: 0.78rem;
}
.inc-source-legend-dot {
  width: 10px;
  height: 10px;
  border-radius: 50%;   /* circle, distinct from the square .legend-swatch in Dashboard.css */
  display: inline-block;
}
.inc-source-legend-dot-manual { background: #199e70; }
.inc-source-legend-dot-fr     { background: #3987e5; }
